---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import Terminal from './Terminal.astro';
---

<Section
  id="remote"
  title="Run the lanes on a VPS, a container or a codespace. It opens no ports."
  reverse
  more={{ href: '/remote/', label: 'More about remote machines' }}
>
  <p>
    Pair once over ssh. Your laptop's daemon then mirrors the remote hostnames and ports, same
    names, same numbers, so the URL a service prints there is the one you open here, with the
    certificate you already trust.
  </p>
  <p>Nothing is published, and the remote machine needs no forwarding enabled.</p>
  <div slot="visual" class="terminal-stack">
    <Terminal title="on my-vps">
      <pre class="terminal-content"><span class="command">$ devlanes daemon pair</span>
pairing code: <span class="url">K7QM-3XWD</span>
it works once and expires in 10 minutes
on your other machine, run:
  devlanes remote connect &lt;box&gt; --code K7QM-3XWD</pre>
    </Terminal>
    <Terminal title="on your laptop">
      <pre class="terminal-content"><span class="command">$ devlanes remote connect my-vps --code K7QM-3XWD</span>
<span class="command">$ devlanes url ls</span>
HOST                      TARGET       PORT   STATE
api.myapp1.localhost  ->  myapp@1:api  20010  <span class="success">ready</span>
myapp1.localhost      ->  myapp@1:web  20011  <span class="success">ready</span></pre>
    </Terminal>
  </div>
</Section>
